  "question": {
    "text": "0.45 gm of an organic compound gave on combustion 0.792 gm of CO<sub>2</sub> and 0.324 gm of water. 0.24 gm of the same substance was Kjeldahlised and the ammonia liberated was absorbed in 50.0 ml of M/8 H<sub>2</sub>SO<sub>4</sub>. The excess acid required 77.0 ml of N/10 NaOH for complete neutralisation. Calculate the empirical formula of the compound."
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "H<sub>4</sub>C<sub>2</sub>N<sub>8</sub>O",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "C<sub>2</sub>H<sub>4</sub>N<sub>8</sub>O",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "C<sub>4</sub>H<sub>8</sub>N<sub>2</sub>O",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "C<sub>2</sub>N<sub>2</sub>H<sub>4</sub>O",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "C"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "Calculation of the percentage composition :<br /><br />i)&nbsp; Percentage of carbon<br /><br />&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<math> <mrow> <mo>=</mo> <mfrac> <mrow> <mn>1</mn> <mn>2</mn> </mrow> <mrow> <mn>4</mn> <mn>4</mn> </mrow> </mfrac> <mo>&times;</mo> <mfrac> <mrow> <msub> <mtext>Mass of CO</mtext> <mn>2</mn> </msub> <mtext>Produced</mtext> </mrow> <mrow> <mtext>Mass of substance taken</mtext> </mrow> </mfrac> <mo>&times;</mo> <mn>1</mn> <mn>0</mn> <mn>0</mn> </mrow> </math><br /><br />&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<math> <mrow> <mo>=</mo> <mfrac> <mrow> <mn>1</mn> <mn>2</mn> </mrow> <mrow> <mn>4</mn> <mn>4</mn> </mrow> </mfrac> <mo>&times;</mo> <mfrac> <mrow> <mn>0</mn> <mtext>.</mtext> <mn>7</mn> <mn>9</mn> <mn>2</mn> </mrow> <mrow> <mn>0</mn> <mtext>.</mtext> <mn>4</mn> <mn>5</mn> </mrow> </mfrac> <mo>&times;</mo> <mn>1</mn> <mn>0</mn> <mn>0</mn> <mo>=</mo> <mn>4</mn> <mn>8</mn> <mtext>.</mtext> <mn>0</mn> </mrow> </math><br /><br />ii)&nbsp; Percentage of hydrogen<br /><br />&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; <math> <mrow> <mo>=</mo> <mfrac> <mrow> <mn>2</mn> </mrow> <mrow> <mn>1</mn> <mn>8</mn> </mrow> </mfrac> <mo>&times;</mo> <mfrac> <mrow> <msub> <mtext>Mass of H</mtext> <mn>2</mn> </msub> <mtext>O produced</mtext> </mrow> <mrow> <mtext>Mass of substance taken</mtext> </mrow> </mfrac> <mo>&times;</mo> <mn>1</mn> <mn>0</mn> <mn>0</mn> </mrow> </math><br /><br />&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<math> <mrow> <mo>=</mo> <mfrac> <mrow> <mn>2</mn> </mrow> <mrow> <mn>1</mn> <mn>8</mn> </mrow> </mfrac> <mo>&times;</mo> <mfrac> <mrow> <mn>0</mn> <mtext>.</mtext> <mn>3</mn> <mn>2</mn> <mn>4</mn> </mrow> <mrow> <mn>0</mn> <mtext>.</mtext> <mn>4</mn> <mn>5</mn> </mrow> </mfrac> <mo>&times;</mo> <mn>1</mn> <mn>0</mn> <mn>0</mn> <mo>=</mo> <mn>8</mn> <mtext>.</mtext> <mn>0</mn> </mrow> </math><br /><br />iii)&nbsp; Percentage of nitrogen<br /><br />mEq. of H<sub>2</sub>SO<sub>4</sub> <math> <mrow> <mo>=</mo> <mn>5</mn> <mn>0</mn> <mo>&times;</mo> <mfrac> <mrow> <mtext>M</mtext> </mrow> <mrow> <mn>8</mn> </mrow> </mfrac> <mo>&times;</mo> <mn>2</mn> <mo>=</mo> <mn>1</mn> <mn>2</mn> <mtext>.</mtext> <mn>5</mn> </mrow> </math><br /><br />mEq. of NaOH <math> <mrow> <mo>=</mo> <mn>7</mn> <mn>2</mn> <mo>&times;</mo> <mfrac> <mrow> <mn>1</mn> </mrow> <mrow> <mn>1</mn> <mn>0</mn> </mrow> </mfrac> <mo>&times;</mo> <mn>1</mn> <mo>=</mo> <mn>7</mn> <mtext>.</mtext> <mn>7</mn> </mrow> </math><br /><br />Excess of H<sub>2</sub>SO<sub>4</sub> used to neutralise ammonia<br /><br />&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; = 12.5 - 7.7 = 4.8<br /><br />Percentage of N<sub>2</sub> <math> <mrow> <mo>=</mo> <mfrac> <mrow> <mn>1</mn> <mtext>.</mtext> <mn>4</mn> <mo>&times;</mo> <mn>4</mn> <mtext>.</mtext> <mn>8</mn> </mrow> <mrow> <mn>0</mn> <mtext>.</mtext> <mn>2</mn> <mn>4</mn> </mrow> </mfrac> <mo>=</mo> <mn>2</mn> <mn>8</mn> <mtext>.</mtext> <mn>0</mn> <mtext>%</mtext> </mrow> </math><br /><br />iv)&nbsp; Percentage of oxygen = 100 - (percentage of C + percentage of H + percentage of N) = 100 - (48.0 + 8.0 + 28.0) = 16.0.<br /><br />b.&nbsp; Calculation of empirical formula :<br /><br />&nbsp;<table align=\"center\" border=\"1\" cellpadding=\"1\" cellspacing=\"1\" style=\"width: 100%;\">\t<thead>\t\t<tr>\t\t\t<th scope=\"col\">Element</th>\t\t\t<th scope=\"col\">Percentage</th>\t\t\t<th scope=\"col\">Atomic mass number of atoms</th>\t\t\t<th scope=\"col\">Relative number of atoms</th>\t\t\t<th scope=\"col\">Simlpest atomic ratio</th>\t\t\t<th scope=\"col\">Simplest whole number atomic ratio</th>\t\t</tr>\t</thead>\t<tbody>\t\t<tr>\t\t\t<td>Carbon</td>\t\t\t<td>48.8</td>\t\t\t<td>12</td>\t\t\t<td><math> <mrow> <mfrac> <mrow> <mn>4</mn> <mn>8</mn> <mtext>.</mtext> <mn>0</mn> </mrow> <mrow> <mn>1</mn> <mn>2</mn> </mrow> </mfrac> <mo>=</mo> <mn>4</mn> </mrow> </math></td>\t\t\t<td><math> <mrow> <mfrac> <mrow> <mn>4</mn> </mrow> <mrow> <mn>1</mn> </mrow> </mfrac> <mo>=</mo> <mn>4</mn> </mrow> </math></td>\t\t\t<td>4</td>\t\t</tr>\t\t<tr>\t\t\t<td>Hydrogen</td>\t\t\t<td>8.0</td>\t\t\t<td>1</td>\t\t\t<td><math> <mrow> <mfrac> <mrow> <mn>8</mn> <mtext>.</mtext> <mn>0</mn> </mrow> <mrow> <mn>1</mn> </mrow> </mfrac> <mo>=</mo> <mn>8</mn> </mrow> </math></td>\t\t\t<td><math> <mrow> <mfrac> <mrow> <mn>8</mn> <mtext>.</mtext> <mn>0</mn> </mrow> <mrow> <mn>1</mn> </mrow> </mfrac> <mo>=</mo> <mn>8</mn> </mrow> </math></td>\t\t\t<td>8</td>\t\t</tr>\t\t<tr>\t\t\t<td>Nitrogen</td>\t\t\t<td>28.0</td>\t\t\t<td>14</td>\t\t\t<td><math> <mrow> <mfrac> <mrow> <mn>2</mn> <mn>8</mn> <mtext>.</mtext> <mn>0</mn> </mrow> <mrow> <mn>1</mn> <mn>4</mn> </mrow> </mfrac> <mo>=</mo> <mn>2</mn> </mrow> </math></td>\t\t\t<td><math> <mrow> <mfrac> <mrow> <mn>2</mn> </mrow> <mrow> <mn>1</mn> </mrow> </mfrac> <mo>=</mo> <mn>2</mn> </mrow> </math></td>\t\t\t<td>2</td>\t\t</tr>\t\t<tr>\t\t\t<td>Oxygen</td>\t\t\t<td>16.0</td>\t\t\t<td>16</td>\t\t\t<td><math> <mrow> <mfrac> <mrow> <mn>1</mn> <mn>6</mn> <mtext>.</mtext> <mn>0</mn> </mrow> <mrow> <mn>1</mn> <mn>6</mn> </mrow> </mfrac> <mo>=</mo> <mn>1</mn> </mrow> </math></td>\t\t\t<td><math> <mrow> <mfrac> <mrow> <mn>1</mn> </mrow> <mrow> <mn>1</mn> </mrow> </mfrac> <mo>=</mo> <mn>1</mn> </mrow> </math></td>\t\t\t<td>1</td>\t\t</tr>\t</tbody></table><br /><br />Hence, the empirical formula of the compound is C<sub>4</sub>H<sub>8</sub>N<sub>2</sub>O."
  }
}